.TH FERRIPRINT 1 "October 2026" "Ferriprint" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ferriprint \- secure driverless IPP frontend for an existing native CUPS queue
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ferriprint
.RB [ --config " PATH"]
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ferriprint validates standard IPP media, margins, quality, tray, color and sides,
including complete named print recipes, against the private PPD and managed
profile. It forwards documents and resolved native options to an existing CUPS
queue. Accounts, printer grants and installed bindings have private managed state.
It does not rasterize documents, install vendor drivers or certify physical output.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The default bootstrap file is ferriprint.toml in the current directory.
The packaged service reads /etc/ferriprint/ferriprint.toml.
Listener, TLS, network/anonymous policy, trusted CUPS server origins and optional
fixed webhook transport belong in the protected startup file. Version0.3 rejects
legacy bootstrap access.users and printers; use the explicit migrate-0.2 import.
Accounts/PHCs and grants live only in state_dir/access.toml; active printer
bindings live only in state_dir/printers.toml. Editable mapping/default/complete
recipe data lives only in state_dir/profiles/NAME.toml. The trusted-source wizard
privately acquires PPDs; neither browser nor CLI configures a native queue.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Validate bootstrap configuration, private PPD and managed profiles offline.
No printer is contacted and no job is submitted.
.TP
.B serve
Start the frontend, probe upstream formats and reconcile durable jobs.
This is the default command when no subcommand is given.
.TP
.B setup
Enumerate, inspect or install an existing queue from a protected trusted CUPS
source, using the same validators/catalog commit as /admin/onboarding.
The install command requires explicit confirmed choices. Consult
.B ferriprint setup --help
for subcommands; no arbitrary URI/PPD-path fallback or driver installation exists.
No setup step submits a print.
.TP
.B user init --username NAME
Initialize the first managed administrator and empty catalog offline as the
intended state owner. Read a hidden terminal or bounded stdin password, never argv.
.TP
.B user recover-admin --username NAME
Offline administrator recovery with the service lock/private-state validators;
not a network backdoor.
.TP
.B migrate-0.2 --output PATH [--credential-sources PATH]
Import legacy users/printers explicitly while stopped, preserving durable job
ownership/identity/defaults. An optional protected TOML password_hash_files map
names exactly all persistent PHC sources when old systemd runtime paths vanished.
Old input is retained; existing destinations/unsafe inputs reject without overwrite.
.TP
.B user password-hash
Auxiliary Argon2id generation from protected stdin/terminal, including preparation
of legacy import sources; not the0.3 runtime account store. Never pass plaintext
credentials in argv, URLs or public configuration.
.TP
.B abandon
Offline escape hatch for a job with unknown upstream submission outcome.
Requires explicit acknowledgement; the real upstream job may still print.
It releases local admission capacity but retains the audit record.
.SH SECURITY
Non-loopback listeners require TLS and explicit client networks.
Discovery visibility never grants access and TLS verification is not disabled.
The configured canonical FQDN must match its certificate.
Authenticated users own their jobs. An IPP requesting-user-name is not a credential.
Explicit anonymous trusted-LAN admission is a shared principal, not per-user isolation.
Administration always requires an authenticated admin role, including when anonymous
IPP printing is enabled. State-changing browser actions require a same-origin
CSRF-protected request.
Ordinary users require current enabled accounts and per-printer grants; admins
have explicit global rights. Suspended/historical usernames cannot be reused.
The final enabled admin cannot be suspended or demoted. Browser users/rights are
managed at /admin/users; own-password changes at /account verify the old password.
.PP
Complete recipes are exposed as standard job-presets-supported collections.
Clients copy their Job Template fields; no job-preset-name selector is invented
and native-dialog visibility is not promised. Explicit supported overrides win.
.PP
The fixed optional webhook transport persists privacy-minimal operational
transitions/outbox/retries. At-least-once delivery requires receiver event-ID
deduplication. Queued is not delivered;2xx is acknowledgement, not proof a human
read a message. Unknown/stale measurements never prove empty paper or recovery.
.PP
Within the existing network/TLS boundary, unauthenticated capability
Get-Printer-Attributes and the corresponding-source offer are permitted.
All job operations, including Validate-Job, and web/job APIs still require a
verified user or an explicitly admitted shared anonymous source.
Invalid supplied credentials always fail, even on those read-only exceptions.
Printer authentication attributes reflect the request source so an existing
anonymous client is not silently forced to authenticate.
.PP
Private keys, password hashes, vendor PPDs and durable job state remain outside
public source/package archives. The service obtains TLS keys through systemd
LoadCredential from operator-managed root-only paths. Never broaden ACME key permissions.
.PP
Legacy import PHCs and optional bearer-secret inputs must be regular,
non-symlink files effectively private to root
and the service UID. Keep originals root0600. A Linux systemd runtime file may
be root0440 with a named service-UID read ACL and no effective group/other access;
the ACL mask is not itself a group grant. No credential-path exemption is used.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ferriprint/ferriprint.toml
Operator-managed static bootstrap configuration; not supplied as an active conffile.
.TP
.I /var/lib/ferriprint
Private accounts/catalog/PPDs/profiles, durable jobs, spool and notification outbox;
retain ownership and all state across upgrades/removal.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/ferriprint
Examples, setup/security/deployment guides, license notices and build metadata.
.SH INSTALLATION
The package does not enable, start or restart the service, import credentials, create a
queue or submit a print. Configure and check first, then explicitly start the
service after reviewing TLS, network admission, ownership and existing jobs.
Package removal refuses to stop an active frontend automatically: gracefully stop
it after checking jobs. Configuration, state and the service account are retained.
.SH SOURCE
The running service exposes the matching AGPL project source archive at /source.
Dependencies are fetched from the committed Cargo.lock; it is not a vendored
or offline dependency source bundle. Release assets include source, SPDX inventory,
checksums and a pinned-input build manifest, not a byte-reproducibility claim.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ipptool (1),
.BR lpstat (1),
.BR systemd.exec (5)
